Implement Upgrade-32 as a bounded PostgreSQL runtime-composition slice for cvsz/zcoder.

Objective: compose the existing EngineeringStore upgrade ledger, PostgreSQL advisory run lease, and monotonic fence into one fail-closed runtime boundary before CLI/backend exposure.

Requirements:
- acquire PostgreSQL advisory exclusivity before issuing a fence generation;
- roll back advisory ownership if fence acquisition fails;
- make the fence token available only during the composed run lease lifetime;
- route EngineeringStoreUpgradeLedger task/control writes through PostgresUpgradeFence.save_task using the current token;
- fail closed for mutation surfaces that would bypass fencing;
- expose a public transactional connection scope from PostgresEngineeringStore instead of using protected connection internals from services;
- add unit tests for ordering, rollback, token lifetime, fenced write routing, fail-closed mutations, reads, and cleanup;
- add live DATABASE_URL integration coverage proving a stale generation cannot create a ledger item through EngineeringStoreUpgradeLedger after a newer owner advances the fence;
- do not expose --state-backend postgres yet;
- preserve Upgrade-20 execution authority, Upgrade-24 budgets, JSON/SQLite behavior, local-only push default, and all CI/security gates.
